1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,690
Hirose?

2
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:11,220
You're not here for work, I take it.

3
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:14,040
Is everything all right?

4
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:17,410
Yes, what brings you here at this hour?

5
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:20,840
This.

6
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,760
You forgot your wallet at the auditorium.

7
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:26,940
I didn't receive a reply when I called,

8
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:30,900
so I thought to check your license,

9
00:00:30,900 --> 00:00:34,770
and make the delivery myself.

10
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:37,880
I apologize for surprising you.

11
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:42,440
No, I'm sorry I made you go out of your way.

12
00:00:42,440 --> 00:00:45,350
Mao... Tsukidome hurt his foot,

13
00:00:45,350 --> 00:00:48,670
so I didn't notice your calls.

14
00:00:48,670 --> 00:00:51,480
I only just finished treating him.

15
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:54,170
I'm terribly sorry for the trouble.

16
00:00:54,170 --> 00:00:58,550
Don't worry, you caused no trouble at all.

17
00:00:58,550 --> 00:01:02,710
Thank you so much.

18
00:02:10,110 --> 00:02:13,520
I hear your birthday is next Thursday?

19
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,850
That's right.

20
00:02:14,850 --> 00:02:16,790
Then we have to celebrate.

21
00:02:16,790 --> 00:02:18,020
Absolutely!

22
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:21,640
I'm sorry, I actually have plans that day.

23
00:02:22,610 --> 00:02:24,020
Oh?

24
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:26,120
"Plans," huh?

25
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:29,010
Not with a lover, of course.

26
00:02:29,010 --> 00:02:30,480
He invited me to dinner

27
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:33,880
without knowing it was my birthday.

28
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:36,330
- Really?
- I see.

29
00:02:36,330 --> 00:02:39,230
Sorry, I have plans Thursday.

30
00:02:39,230 --> 00:02:41,490
Pencil me in for another day.

31
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:45,460
Thanks.

32
00:03:01,910 --> 00:03:04,580
Mao.

33
00:03:07,480 --> 00:03:10,930
Are you free next Thursday?

34
00:03:10,930 --> 00:03:12,640
Huh?

35
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:16,800
My mother taught me her napolitan recipe,

36
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:19,390
and I wanted you to try.

37
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:22,570
Thursday...

38
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:31,190
Mao?

39
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:37,770
Yeah, I'm free.

40
00:03:38,690 --> 00:03:42,060
Great!

41
00:03:42,060 --> 00:03:44,020
Get ready to have your socks blown off,

42
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:47,240
I'll put my all into cooking for you.

43
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,000
Thanks, I will.

44
00:04:02,270 --> 00:04:03,850
Mao.

45
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:08,350
How long have you been there?

46
00:04:08,350 --> 00:04:10,550
Doesn't matter, right?

47
00:04:10,550 --> 00:04:12,780
You scare me sometimes.

48
00:04:12,780 --> 00:04:16,800
I hear Thursday is Monou's birthday.

49
00:04:19,060 --> 00:04:23,050
- Really?
- Don't bother, I can tell you knew.

50
00:04:28,210 --> 00:04:32,860
You said you'd treat Nana well.
I can trust you on that, right?

51
00:04:37,590 --> 00:04:39,230
Of course.

52
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:48,410
If you realize you can't be there for her,

53
00:04:48,410 --> 00:04:51,170
then I'm going after her myself.

54
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:57,130
I'm serious about her.

55
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,080
See you around.

56
00:05:07,100 --> 00:05:08,340
[Obstetrics and gynecology]

57
00:05:08,340 --> 00:05:10,100
Ms. Yamaguchi?

58
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:11,930
We're ready for you.

59
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:13,910
We meet again.

60
00:05:13,910 --> 00:05:15,400
Getting another check up?

61
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:17,440
Hello! Yes, I am.

62
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:19,650
Is your due date coming up?

63
00:05:19,650 --> 00:05:21,550
Yes. I'm expecting next month, on the 7th.

64
00:05:21,550 --> 00:05:24,220
Boy or girl?

65
00:05:24,220 --> 00:05:26,450
Girl.

66
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:32,130
I also have a daughter.

67
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:35,750
Though I've caused her nothing but trouble,

68
00:05:35,750 --> 00:05:39,310
I'm truly glad she was born.

69
00:05:42,150 --> 00:05:45,660
I'm itching to meet my child as well.

70
00:05:45,660 --> 00:05:47,610
Babies are so wonderful.

71
00:05:47,610 --> 00:05:51,570
Just seeing them makes everyone happy.

72
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:03,350
Ma'am, are you all right?

73
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:07,910
I'm sorry. Was I looking glum?

74
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:12,830
I've had to frequent the hospital these days,

75
00:06:12,830 --> 00:06:18,870
and I worry I'm troubling my daughter...

76
00:06:20,050 --> 00:06:23,520
I'm being quite the burden to her.

77
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,280
If I were in her shoes,

78
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:35,140
I wouldn't think you were a burden.

79
00:06:37,560 --> 00:06:41,110
You are her mother.

80
00:06:41,110 --> 00:06:44,110
Nothing would make your daughter happier

81
00:06:44,110 --> 00:06:47,170
than seeing her mother healthy again.

82
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:50,100
You think so?

83
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:51,790
I do.

84
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:54,360
Thank you.

85
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:56,330
Of course.

86
00:06:59,580 --> 00:07:02,620
Come into this world safely.

87
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:04,080
And you take care, dear.

88
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:06,840
Thank you.

89
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:17,270
Sis!

90
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,920
Sorry I'm late.

91
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,040
No worries.

92
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,230
It is almost your turn?

93
00:07:22,230 --> 00:07:24,640
- "Sis"?
- I think I'm after this next patient.

94
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:26,720
Sounds good.

95
00:07:26,720 --> 00:07:28,650
That's her younger sister?

96
00:07:30,650 --> 00:07:32,800
Misaki.

97
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:36,640
Misaki?

98
00:07:37,660 --> 00:07:40,680
Sorry, what's up?

99
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:42,450
Everything all right?

100
00:07:42,450 --> 00:07:43,750
You seem tired.

101
00:07:43,750 --> 00:07:45,730
I'm fine.

102
00:07:45,730 --> 00:07:49,640
When do you think you'll be discharged?

103
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:53,050
The doctors say
I'll be let out early this time.

104
00:07:53,050 --> 00:07:55,750
Really? I'm glad to hear it.

105
00:07:55,750 --> 00:07:57,970
<i>Is she packed for the hospital?</i>
[Erika Katsuragawa]

106
00:07:57,970 --> 00:08:00,150
<i>She should get that prepped now.</i>

107
00:08:00,150 --> 00:08:02,400
I think she was, but...

108
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:04,010
- Rin.
- Yeah?

109
00:08:04,010 --> 00:08:05,260
Are you packed for the hospital?

110
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:07,590
Yeah. My bags are by the front door.

111
00:08:07,590 --> 00:08:09,150
Did you hear that?

112
00:08:09,150 --> 00:08:11,520
<i>I did.</i>

113
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:14,240
She apparently feels too heavy to move.

114
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:17,150
<i>That doesn't surprise me.</i>

115
00:08:17,150 --> 00:08:18,870
<i>Can you pass the phone to Rin?</i>

116
00:08:18,870 --> 00:08:21,130
<i>I promised to give her some baby supplies.</i>

117
00:08:21,130 --> 00:08:22,870
Sure.

118
00:08:22,870 --> 00:08:24,500
- Here.
- <i>Hello?</i>

119
00:08:24,500 --> 00:08:25,970
Hey, Erika.

120
00:08:25,970 --> 00:08:27,250
<i>'Sup.</i>

121
00:08:27,250 --> 00:08:28,740
'Sup.

122
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:30,080
<i>How're you feeling?</i>

123
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:32,870
Better these days.

124
00:08:34,400 --> 00:08:38,410
Rin's really going to be a mom, isn't she...

125
00:08:38,410 --> 00:08:40,980
All right, thanks.

126
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:43,480
Talk to you later.

127
00:08:44,510 --> 00:08:46,720
Thanks.

128
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:50,920
I feel so heavy...

129
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:52,060
You okay?

130
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:57,050
Yeah. She had not been kicking,

131
00:08:57,050 --> 00:08:59,950
maybe because it's tight in there?

132
00:08:59,950 --> 00:09:02,220
But today she's moving like crazy.

133
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:05,520
She's happy you're here.

134
00:09:05,520 --> 00:09:09,580
Must be because I help her mom take it easy.

135
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:12,930
We appreciate a sister we can rely on, right?

136
00:09:14,090 --> 00:09:17,990
Rin looked overjoyed.

137
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:20,000
I'm happy for her.

138
00:09:25,070 --> 00:09:29,680
Happiness comes in many forms.

139
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:35,410
But the joy she's acquired

140
00:09:35,410 --> 00:09:40,470
is something very substantial.

141
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:44,690
Yeah.

142
00:09:44,690 --> 00:09:48,150
I've thought about
whether I want a child or not.

143
00:09:49,970 --> 00:09:53,500
But I don't know what it is I want,

144
00:09:53,500 --> 00:09:55,970
no matter how much I ponder it.

145
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:04,590
I understand giving birth
may be difficult for me.

146
00:10:04,590 --> 00:10:07,550
Even so, I can't definitively say
I don't want children.

147
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:10,920
I know.

148
00:10:17,170 --> 00:10:19,040
Erika.

149
00:10:20,350 --> 00:10:24,140
I expected to fall in love, get married,

150
00:10:25,350 --> 00:10:31,040
and one day have a child,
like every other family.

151
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:36,250
But if I'm unable to conceive,

152
00:10:38,020 --> 00:10:44,320
I'm depriving my future partner

153
00:10:46,190 --> 00:10:51,120
of that opportunity.

154
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:55,540
If that's the consequence...

155
00:10:59,710 --> 00:11:03,310
then I should give up on marriage.

156
00:11:04,490 --> 00:11:08,900
I should give up on romance entirely.

157
00:11:12,910 --> 00:11:15,500
I'm less bothered by the fact
that I can't give birth.

158
00:11:17,270 --> 00:11:21,110
Rather, I'm more upset I can't give anyone

159
00:11:22,510 --> 00:11:24,420
the happiness they'd expect from a family.

160
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:30,660
And yet, I...

161
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:34,210
Even though I know it's impossible, I...

162
00:11:43,410 --> 00:11:47,660
Happiness is a difficult thing, isn't it?

163
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:07,490
Sui. There's something I haven't told you

164
00:12:09,170 --> 00:12:11,770
because I didn't want you to judge us.

165
00:12:17,330 --> 00:12:20,540
My husband was also infertile.

166
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:28,950
The doctors said our chances
were practically zero.

167
00:12:31,340 --> 00:12:35,860
But I never once thought of leaving him.

168
00:12:40,650 --> 00:12:44,120
I love my husband, first and foremost.

169
00:12:44,120 --> 00:12:46,880
Children was only an option, not a necessity.

170
00:12:48,770 --> 00:12:50,990
My husband...

171
00:12:52,530 --> 00:12:56,090
Although he was told our chances were low,

172
00:12:56,090 --> 00:12:58,540
we were ultimately blessed with a chance.

173
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:02,530
What I'm trying to say is...

174
00:13:02,530 --> 00:13:04,840
Practically zero
doesn't mean impossible, okay?

175
00:13:07,080 --> 00:13:10,390
I won't pretend to understand
what you're going through.

176
00:13:10,390 --> 00:13:14,780
But wanting a child is a choice
between you and your partner.

177
00:13:15,980 --> 00:13:19,050
So, once you've fallen in love,

178
00:13:19,050 --> 00:13:22,210
don't ponder over that question alone.

179
00:13:22,210 --> 00:13:26,260
Talk it out with your partner.

180
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:37,860
Whether you mention your infertility or not
is entirely your choice.

181
00:13:37,860 --> 00:13:42,570
Just like how it's your partner's choice
to decide how to respond.

182
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,970
I suppose so.

183
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,550
Thank you.

184
00:13:59,550 --> 00:14:01,410
Enjoy.

185
00:14:03,410 --> 00:14:05,360
Everything was so delicious.

186
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:08,780
I'm glad you enjoyed it.

187
00:14:09,490 --> 00:14:12,660
But I'm surprised we came back here.

188
00:14:12,660 --> 00:14:14,170
Why?

189
00:14:14,170 --> 00:14:17,530
I love this place so much,
I may become a regular.

190
00:14:17,530 --> 00:14:21,010
I'm honored you feel that way.

191
00:14:29,290 --> 00:14:31,920
This is for you.

192
00:14:32,670 --> 00:14:35,080
What's the occasion?

193
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:38,400
Happy birthday.

194
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:40,840
How did you know?

195
00:14:43,810 --> 00:14:48,830
When I checked your license,
I happened to see your date of birth.

196
00:14:49,450 --> 00:14:51,530
Oh, thank you.

197
00:14:51,530 --> 00:14:57,740
Your sincerity and attitude toward work

198
00:14:57,740 --> 00:15:00,060
truly inspire me.

199
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:04,930
Though I invited you today
without knowing it was your birthday,

200
00:15:04,930 --> 00:15:08,980
I'm glad we could celebrate
your special day together.

201
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:18,010
Open it, if you'd like.

202
00:15:18,010 --> 00:15:19,590
Then I will.

203
00:15:39,060 --> 00:15:41,250
A tumbler...

204
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:48,260
It's good.

205
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:49,750
Really?

206
00:15:49,750 --> 00:15:51,650
Yes!

207
00:15:53,260 --> 00:15:58,470
The pasta's perfectly al dente, too.
This may be the best napolitan I've ever had.

208
00:16:00,800 --> 00:16:03,180
My mother taught me
how to boil them just right.

209
00:16:03,180 --> 00:16:05,230
I see.

210
00:16:09,630 --> 00:16:13,570
She wants to meet you one day.

211
00:16:21,140 --> 00:16:23,200
Monou...

212
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:27,500
She is celebrating today, yes?

213
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:30,880
Maybe she's getting dinner with Hirose.

214
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:36,410
Possibly.

215
00:16:42,580 --> 00:16:45,070
Thank you for dinner.

216
00:16:45,070 --> 00:16:46,870
And the birthday gift as well.

217
00:16:46,870 --> 00:16:49,830
I'm glad you like it.

218
00:16:54,170 --> 00:16:56,010
Hirose?

219
00:16:57,520 --> 00:16:59,310
Monou.

220
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:00,960
Yes?

221
00:17:02,430 --> 00:17:08,780
Earlier, I said I was inspired
by your work ethic.

222
00:17:09,790 --> 00:17:11,480
But...

223
00:17:13,780 --> 00:17:15,890
Truthfully, that's not all.

224
00:17:20,870 --> 00:17:23,000
I feel as though...

225
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:27,420
we can share a future ambition together.

226
00:17:28,850 --> 00:17:30,970
No, I sincerely believe it.

227
00:17:32,380 --> 00:17:35,360
I won't ask for anything immediate.

228
00:17:35,360 --> 00:17:38,090
But won't you look my way as well?

229
00:17:44,600 --> 00:17:46,680
I can wash the rest.

230
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:49,620
It's fine, I've got it. Leave it there.

231
00:17:55,970 --> 00:17:58,200
- <i>Then could you grab the plates?</i>
- <i>Sure.</i>

232
00:18:01,920 --> 00:18:04,730
<i>It just split in half.</i>

233
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:12,710
I had fun today.

234
00:18:12,710 --> 00:18:15,120
It was nice, spending time together.

235
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:18,070
I'm glad to hear it.

236
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:20,360
Really.

237
00:18:21,800 --> 00:18:23,780
I had fun.

238
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:27,370
But...

239
00:18:31,410 --> 00:18:33,000
But...

240
00:18:38,760 --> 00:18:41,250
Mao.

241
00:18:41,250 --> 00:18:43,140
I'm sorry.

242
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:47,420
I'd like to break up.

243
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:50,120
What?

244
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:53,360
I...

245
00:18:54,630 --> 00:18:57,890
I knew today was Monou's birthday.

246
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:04,630
But Mao, you're so kind.

247
00:19:04,630 --> 00:19:07,350
And because you're kind,

248
00:19:07,350 --> 00:19:12,070
you entertain my whims.

249
00:19:14,470 --> 00:19:16,890
I didn't care if it was out of pity.

250
00:19:16,890 --> 00:19:19,330
I just wanted your attention.

251
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:23,460
I guess...

252
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:30,710
I was far greedier than I thought I was.

253
00:19:31,550 --> 00:19:35,200
<i>Whenever you showed care for Monou,</i>

254
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:37,860
<i>I could tell the difference between us.</i>

255
00:19:39,310 --> 00:19:41,990
I thought I wouldn't mind your kindness

256
00:19:41,990 --> 00:19:45,960
even if it were out of pity.

257
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:56,230
But I'm at my limit.

258
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:58,690
I'm so sorry.

259
00:20:09,660 --> 00:20:11,860
I'm sorry.

260
00:20:21,090 --> 00:20:25,870
I wasn't ever kind to you.

261
00:20:31,110 --> 00:20:33,870
I cared for you...

262
00:20:35,420 --> 00:20:38,800
I rescued you...

263
00:20:41,390 --> 00:20:44,300
All for my own sake.

264
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:56,050
When I was a kid,
I couldn't protect someone I cared about.

265
00:20:56,050 --> 00:20:58,000
So, growing up,

266
00:20:59,720 --> 00:21:03,200
I was desperate to protect
anyone I came across.

267
00:21:09,220 --> 00:21:12,040
I wanted to alleviate
my regret from that day.

268
00:21:15,340 --> 00:21:20,910
And now my selfish motives have hurt you.

269
00:21:32,390 --> 00:21:34,610
Everything I've done...

270
00:21:37,630 --> 00:21:43,380
was an insult to your feelings for me.

271
00:21:48,950 --> 00:21:51,250
Then count me equally as guilty.

272
00:21:52,870 --> 00:21:57,570
I knew you wouldn't let me go,

273
00:21:58,370 --> 00:22:04,720
seeing how weak I was in the moment.

274
00:22:05,910 --> 00:22:10,720
But I don't regret a thing.

275
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:14,990
Because...

276
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:21,630
I still wanted you, despite it all.

277
00:22:27,310 --> 00:22:29,010
Mizuno...

278
00:22:31,430 --> 00:22:33,180
Mao.

279
00:22:34,830 --> 00:22:37,980
Will you leave things as is

280
00:22:37,980 --> 00:22:40,250
with Monou?

281
00:22:49,620 --> 00:22:51,740
<i>I won't ask for anything immediate.</i>

282
00:22:51,740 --> 00:22:54,490
<i>But won't you look my way as well?</i>

283
00:22:58,750 --> 00:23:02,520
What is it I want to do?

284
00:23:15,180 --> 00:23:18,370
[Obstetrics and gynecology]

285
00:23:18,370 --> 00:23:19,460
Thank you.

286
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:21,860
Take care.

287
00:23:21,860 --> 00:23:26,160
You're Sui Monou's younger sister, yes?

288
00:23:26,990 --> 00:23:29,230
Pardon?

289
00:23:29,230 --> 00:23:33,470
Say, did your sister tell you her secret?

290
00:23:34,850 --> 00:23:38,030
Her secret?

291
00:23:45,530 --> 00:23:49,120
I don't think I'll meet
an individual like him again.

292
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:51,100
You love Sui, don't you?

293
00:23:51,100 --> 00:23:54,010
Please make Monou happy.

294
00:23:54,010 --> 00:23:56,770
She must be so jealous

295
00:23:56,770 --> 00:23:58,400
you're pregnant.

296
00:23:58,400 --> 00:24:00,000
I'm the worst.

